      "value": "Official Worlds would be nice, but I would never restrict access to those worlds as it wouldn't allow new people to join. Even if they haven't uploaded anything doesn't mean they aren't interested in it. They could also be limited because of the Trust System.\n\nThere are however two worlds being created (unofficially) that would fit under these categories, but they aren't ready for public just yet.\n\nBut I would suggest joining the two events that currently are going, as it is a good way to join in the development of something. Both are good events for new & advanced users.\nThese events are a good place to discuss and show what you currently are working on. Even get help/tips on how to get started or do certain things and feedback on what you have made. It's also a good place to do a performance test of your creation.\n\nDeveloper Meetup (World Developers) hosted by Squid\nEvery Sunday 10PM UTC\n\nAvatar Development hosted by Ghoster\nEvery Saturday 6PM UTC\n\nhttp://vrchatevents.com/",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
